    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> respectively, be the transverse and conjugate axes of the hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Then the area of the region above the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, below the transverse axis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and on the right of the conjugate axis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is:"
